        "original_id": "b819b3f1-6af5-5bb2-8078-39fc8f75acd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Julian Marley\n- Concepts: Rastafari, roots reggae\n- Products: A Time & Place\n- Companies: Lightyear Entertainment\n- Places: Jamaica\n\nFacts:\n- Rastafari is classified as a new religious movement that developed in Jamaica during the 1930s.\n- Roots reggae is a subgenre of reggae that addresses artists’ everyday lives and aspirations, including Rastafari spirituality and the honoring of God as Jah.\n- Julian Marley follows in his father’s footsteps and is a devout Rastafarian who uses his music to inspire his life and spirituality.\n- A Time & Place is the second studio album by reggae artist Julian Marley, and it was released in 2003 on Lightyear Entertainment.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
